      "source_url": "https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-revised-code/section-4510.14",
      "term": "Jail"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(4) \"Mandatory jail term\" means the mandatory term in jail of three, ten, or thirty consecutive days that must be imposed under division (B)(1), (2), or (3) of this section upon an offender convicted of a violation of division (A) of this section and in relation to which all of the following apply:\n\n(a) Except as specifically authorized under this section, the term must be served in a jail.\n\n(b) Except as specifically authorized under this section, the term cannot be suspended, reduced, or otherwise modified pursuant to any provision of the Revised Code.",
